  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government branch of the state of Arkansas that is responsible for overseeing the legal system in the state. The Sheridan County Court of Circumstances and Municipal Districts makes decisions regarding cases where the county and land areas within the litigation area is decided. The purposes of the Sheridan County Court are to administer justice within the region in which it is located and oversee penalties stemming from the adjudication of these cases. The Court is one of the state legislature's courts and, without the approval of the Governor, may in fact work independently of the state legislature. While the three judges that constitute the Court are a reflection of the population within the local territory, Lawpro.org, by Prof Rod G",
